<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of Cúcuta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1821">1821</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congress of Cúcuta was the constituent assembly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia, meeting at Villa del Rosario de Cúcuta from May to October 1821. It joined Venezuela and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a> in a centralised republic, adopted the Constitution of 1821, elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> president and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-paula-santander">Francisco de Paula Santander</a> vice-president, and passed a law freeing children born to enslaved mothers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-cucuta.jpg" alt="Congress of Cúcuta" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ruben Valero · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Templo_Hist%C3%B3rico_en_C%C3%BAcuta.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
